└── package.json

Key Modules to Build
1. Conversation Model (MongoDB)
Stores user ID, array of messages (role: user/assistant, content, timestamp), and token count used.
2. OpenAI Service
Takes user message + previous messages array, calls gpt-3.5-turbo with a system prompt like "You are a helpful customer support agent.", returns the AI reply.
3. Rate Limiter Middleware
Each user gets max 20 requests/hour stored in Redis. If exceeded, return 429 Too Many Requests.
4. Token Tracker
After each OpenAI response, read usage.total_tokens from the API response and save it to the conversation document. This lets you monitor cost per user.
5. Fallback Logic
If OpenAI returns an error or confidence is low (you detect this by checking if the response contains phrases like "I don't know" or "I'm not sure"), return a pre-written fallback message like "Our team will contact you shortly."
6. Auth Middleware
Standard JWT — user logs in, gets token, passes it in every chat request header.

APIs to Build
MethodRoutePurposePOST/api/auth/registerRegister userPOST/api/auth/loginLogin, get JWTPOST/api/chat/messageSend message, get AI replyGET/api/chat/historyGet conversation historyDELETE/api/chat/historyClear conversation

.env Variables Needed
PORT=5000
MONGO_URI=your_mongodb_uri
JWT_SECRET=your_secret
OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_key
REDIS_URL=your_redis_url
